{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"110480","commit":"9b7db8d998e7c07ef5db93de6fcdb18053452636","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The introduction of `TYPECAST_SPACER`, `escapeTypecast`, and `unescapeTypecast` methods is intended to handle typecasts in CSV headers that contain the delimiter `::`. However, the implementation does not account for potential edge cases where the placeholder `__TYPECAST__` might appear naturally in the data. This could lead to incorrect parsing if the data itself contains `__TYPECAST__`.  \n[Symptom] -\u003e [Technical Cause] -\u003e [Systemic Risk]: Incorrect parsing of CSV headers containing `__TYPECAST__` -\u003e The placeholder `__TYPECAST__` is used without checking for its presence in the data -\u003e Data integrity and correctness are compromised.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/qa/testFixtures/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/CsvTestUtils.java-DST-ADDITION-19594-19655-FieldDeclaration","path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/qa/testFixtures/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/CsvTestUtils.java","srcDst":"DST","content":"private static final String TYPECAST_SPACER \u003d \"__TYPECAST__\";","nodeType":"ADDITION","treeType":"FieldDeclaration","descendantSimpleNames":["String","TYPECAST_SPACER"],"identifiers":["TYPECAST_SPACER"],"startLine":400,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":400,"endLineOffset":65,"length":62,"subs":[]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/qa/testFixtures/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/CsvTestUtils.java-DST-ADDITION-19661-19778-MethodDeclaration","path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/qa/testFixtures/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/CsvTestUtils.java","srcDst":"DST","content":"private static String escapeTypecast(String typecast) {\n        return typecast.replace(\"::\", TYPECAST_SPACER);\n    }","nodeType":"ADDITION","treeType":"MethodDeclaration","descendantSimpleNames":["String","escapeTypecast","String","typecast","typecast","replace","TYPECAST_SPACER"],"identifiers":["escapeTypecast","